# Keep line endings stable across machines.
#
# core.autocrlf (on by default on Windows) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout,
# which changes a file's bytes without changing its content. For most sources
# that is harmless, but:
#   *.sql - db/migrate.py checksums applied migrations; a byte change looked
#           like an edited migration and aborted the runner.
#   *.sh  - /bin/sh refuses scripts whose lines end in CR ("bad interpreter").
# Both are checked out with LF everywhere.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
